@page "/docs/primitives/csp-provider"

<DocsPage Title="CSP Provider" Description="Configures CSP-related behavior for inline tags rendered by the primitives.">
    <p>
        <code>CspProvider</code> cascades a Content Security Policy nonce to the components inside it. The primitives
        themselves never inject <code>&lt;style&gt;</code> or <code>&lt;script&gt;</code> elements: their browser-side styles
        are set through the CSSOM, which CSP allows, and their scripts are ES modules loaded from the package's static assets.
        So nothing in the package needs the nonce today. It's there, as <code>CspSettings</code>, for parts you build that do.
    </p>
    <p>
        Some parts render inline <code>style</code> attributes (positions and sizes), which need
        <code>style-src-attr 'unsafe-inline'</code> under a strict policy, since Blazor sets them as attributes.
    </p>
    <DocsHeading Title="Anatomy" />
    <CodeFigure Code="@Anatomy" />
    <DocsHeading Title="API Reference" />
    <PartReference Type="typeof(CspProvider)" />
    <PartReference Type="typeof(CspSettings)" />
</DocsPage>

@code {
    private const string Anatomy = """
        @using Blazix.Primitives

        <CspProvider Nonce="@nonce">
            ...
        </CspProvider>
        """;
}
